## Security Headers

### Security Headers Middleware
```go
func SecurityHeaders() fiber.Handler {
    return func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
        // Prevent clickjacking
        c.Set("X-Frame-Options", "DENY")

        // Prevent MIME type sniffing
        c.Set("X-Content-Type-Options", "nosniff")

        // Enable XSS protection
        c.Set("X-XSS-Protection", "1; mode=block")

        // Strict transport security (for HTTPS)
        c.Set("Strict-Transport-Security", "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains")

        // Content security policy
        c.Set("Content-Security-Policy", "default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'")

        return c.Next()
    }
}
```

## Logging and Monitoring

### Security Event Logging
```go
type SecurityLogger struct {
    logFile *os.File
    mutex   sync.Mutex
}

type SecurityEvent struct {
    Timestamp time.Time `json:"timestamp"`
    EventType string    `json:"eventType"`
    UserID    string    `json:"userId,omitempty"`
    IP        string    `json:"ip"`
    Details   string    `json:"details"`
    Severity  string    `json:"severity"`
}

func (sl *SecurityLogger) LogSecurityEvent(event SecurityEvent) {
    sl.mutex.Lock()
    defer sl.mutex.Unlock()

    event.Timestamp = time.Now()
    jsonData, _ := json.Marshal(event)

    // Log to file
    sl.logFile.WriteString(string(jsonData) + "\n")
    sl.logFile.Sync()

    // In production, also send to monitoring system
    // monitoring.SendSecurityAlert(event)
}
```

These security patterns ensure the Web-SCP application handles sensitive operations safely and maintains user data protection.